Quickstart Instructions:

Modern macOS and Linux systems:

1) Install a C compiler and make (Xcode Command Line Tools on macOS).
2) cd coding/src
3) Edit include/config.h, especially CODING_ROOT, CODING_BACKUPS and ports.
4) make
5) make install

The Makefile detects macOS and avoids historical Linux-only linker flags.
On Linux, install the system's libcrypt development package if it is not
already available.  The resulting programs are summink, angel, ident and
intercom.  The server still expects to be started from its configured ROOT
directory.  The build now creates the empty runtime directories omitted by
the historical source archive.

Original instructions:

1) cd coding/src
1) edit include/config.h for your system, environment, and required
   options.
2) edit Makefile for your system.
3) make
4) make install
5) ../bin/angel &

Oh, and do remember to strip tested binaries when you're happy that your
program is stable enough to no longer require debug information.
6) strip ../bin/summink

Have fun :-)
